


=DB Stats=

==Description==

The DB Stats application shows the per-query usage statistics collected by SaltOS4 when the debug/slowquerystats configuration flag is enabled.
It tracks, for each distinct query call site, how many times it was executed and how much time it took, allowing developers to spot usage
patterns such as repeated queries (N+1 issues) while debugging.

This data is stored in its own isolated SQLite file, separate from the main application database, and the list is empty until the
debug/slowquerystats flag has been enabled and the application has processed some queries.

==List view==

[../../../../../ujest/snaps/test-screenshots-js-screenshots-common-dbstats-list-en-us-light-1-snap.png]

The following fields are displayed in the list view:

- Source: Call site (file, line and function) that executed the query.
- Count: Number of times this query was executed.
- Avg: Average execution time, in seconds.
- Sum: Total accumulated execution time, in seconds.


==View entry==

This view shows detailed information about a single query call site.

[../../../../../ujest/snaps/test-screenshots-js-screenshots-common-dbstats-view-1-en-us-light-1-snap.png]

It includes:

- Source: Call site (file, line and function) that executed the query.
- Count: Number of times this query was executed.
- Min: Fastest recorded execution time, in seconds.
- Max: Slowest recorded execution time, in seconds.
- Avg: Average execution time, in seconds.
- Sum: Total accumulated execution time, in seconds.
- Datetime: Date and time of the last recorded execution.


==Delete==

DB stats entries cannot be deleted individually from this application; they are only reset by clearing the underlying SQLite file.
